---

## 3. Sentencias Ejecutadas

Transacción atómica ejecutada con el rol `postgres`:

```sql
BEGIN;

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS progress_reports_unique_period
  ON progress_reports (student_id, period_type, period_start, period_end)
  WHERE is_test = false AND status <> 'rejected';

ALTER TABLE progress_reports
  DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS progress_reports_period_type_check,
  ADD CONSTRAINT progress_reports_period_type_check
  CHECK (period_type IN ('mensual', 'trimestral', 'avance', 'cierre_ciclo'));

COMMIT;
```

---

## 4. Evidencia de Verificación Posterior

### 4.1 Definición del CHECK constraint
```sql
SELECT conname, pg_get_constraintdef(oid) AS check_def
FROM pg_constraint
WHERE conname = 'progress_reports_period_type_check';
```
Salida obtenida:
```json
[
  {
    "conname": "progress_reports_period_type_check",
    "check_def": "CHECK ((period_type = ANY (ARRAY['mensual'::text, 'trimestral'::text, 'avance'::text, 'cierre_ciclo'::text])))"
  }
]
```

### 4.2 Definición del Índice Único Parcial
```sql
SELECT indexname, indexdef
FROM pg_indexes
WHERE tablename = 'progress_reports' AND indexname = 'progress_reports_unique_period';
```
Salida obtenida:
```json
[
  {
    "indexname": "progress_reports_unique_period",
    "indexdef": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX progress_reports_unique_period ON public.progress_reports USING btree (student_id, period_type, period_start, period_end) WHERE ((is_test = false) AND (status <> 'rejected'::text))"
  }
]
```

### 4.3 Total de informes en tabla
